<body>
<h1>Product Requirement Document (PRD)</h1>
<div class='meta'>
<strong>Project:</strong> SurakshaGrid — AI Flood Digital Twin & Incident Command System<br/>
<strong>Mission:</strong> Bharat Shakti Mission<br/>
<strong>Version:</strong> 1.0.0 | <strong>Format:</strong> Executive Specification
</div>
<h2>1. Executive Summary & Objective</h2>
<p>SurakshaGrid is a unified real-time incident command system and predictive digital twin designed to mitigate urban and river basin flood disasters. The platform bridges the gap between raw hydrological satellite feeds, predictive machine learning models, tactical rescue route optimization, and emergency citizen telemetry.</p>
<h2>2. Technology Stack Architecture</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technologies & Frameworks</th><th>Core Functionality</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Frontend Web & Mobile</strong></td><td>Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, MapLibre GL</td><td>Citizen Mobile SOS portal, Responsive Officer Command Dashboard, Vector GIS rendering.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Backend & Ingestion</strong></td><td>Python, FastAPI, WebSockets</td><td>High-throughput asynchronous API gateway, real-time SOS stream processing, auth middleware.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Spatial Database</strong></td><td>PostgreSQL, PostGIS, pgRouting</td><td>Geospatial persistence, point-in-polygon queries, geofencing boundaries, incident logs.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Routing Engine</strong></td><td>OpenStreetMap (OSM), OSRM</td><td>Dynamic road network analysis, flood-evasive routing, NDRF boat/vehicle dispatch corridors.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>ML Inundation Engine</strong></td><td>Python, Pandas, XGBoost</td><td>Precipitation-to-inundation risk classification, depth estimation, threshold alerting.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Remote Sensing</strong></td><td>Python, GeoPandas, Rasterio, Sentinel-1 SAR</td><td>Processing Synthetic Aperture Radar imagery through cloud cover to extract surface water extent.</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>3. Target User Personas</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Stranded Citizen (Mobile Web Portal):</strong> Low-friction emergency reporting interface; zero login barrier; automated GPS location fix; one-tap emergency category selection.</li>
<li><strong>EOC Command Officer (NDRF / SDMA):</strong> Authenticated access; high-resolution situational GIS Digital Twin; live incident tracking; real-time route generation avoiding inundated road nodes.</li>
<li><strong>Tactical Rescue Field Operator:</strong> Receives turn-by-turn dynamic safe corridors calculated via OSRM, updated as flood boundaries expand.</li>
</ul>
<h2>4. Functional Requirements</h2>
<h3>4.1. Citizen Mobile SOS Module</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-1.1 Geolocation Acquisition:</strong> Automatically capture high-precision GPS coordinates (lat, lng, accuracy) via HTML5 Geolocation API.</li>
<li><strong>FR-1.2 Incident Triage:</strong> Single-touch incident severity selection (CRITICAL_TRAPPED, MEDICAL_EVAC, FOOD_WATER).</li>
<li><strong>FR-1.3 Low-Bandwidth Telemetry:</strong> Submit payload via lightweight JSON to FastAPI /api/v1/sos endpoint.</li>
<li><strong>FR-1.4 Offline Handling:</strong> Provide immediate local dispatch confirmation and cache payloads locally if connectivity drops.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.2. Geospatial Digital Twin & Vector Map (MapLibre + PostGIS)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-2.1 Dynamic Inundation Layer:</strong> Render real-time flood polygons generated by Rasterio/GeoPandas SAR extraction pipelines.</li>
<li><strong>FR-2.2 Real-time Distress Markers:</strong> Plot incoming citizen SOS incidents as interactive priority-coded markers.</li>
<li><strong>FR-2.3 Live River Sensor Telemetry:</strong> Display IoT water level gauges and threshold indicators over basin sectors.</li>
<li><strong>FR-2.4 Geofenced Evacuation Polygons:</strong> Compute and display dynamic containment zones using PostGIS spatial queries.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.3. Predictive Hydrological Engine (Pandas + XGBoost)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-3.1 Risk Scoring:</strong> Predict 6–12 hour flood inundation probabilities across sub-catchment zones based on live precipitation, soil saturation, and discharge rates.</li>
<li><strong>FR-3.2 Depth & Velocity Estimates:</strong> Output estimated water level rise per grid cell to classify passable vs. impassable roads.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.4. Tactical Evacuation & Rescue Dispatch (OSRM + OSM)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-4.1 Dynamic Obstacle Injection:</strong> Inject flood polygons into OSRM routing weights to penalize or block submerged roads.</li>
<li><strong>FR-4.2 Green Corridor Generation:</strong> Compute optimal, flood-evasive routes between NDRF staging bases and active SOS clusters.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.5. Officer Authentication & Gateway Access</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-5.1 Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Restrict command actions behind JWT-authenticated officer logins.</li>
<li><strong>FR-5.2 Quick Demo Bypass:</strong> Provide isolated mock tokens for evaluation and field simulation modes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>5. Data Flow & System Pipeline</h2>
<pre>
[ Sentinel-1 SAR Radar ] ---> [ Rasterio / GeoPandas ] ---+
                                                          |
[ Live Rain & Gauge APIs ] -> [ XGBoost Flood Engine ] ---+---> [ PostGIS / PostgreSQL ]
                                                          |               |
[ Citizen Mobile SOS ] -----> [ FastAPI Gateway ] --------+               |
                                                                          v
                                                               [ Next.js + MapLibre ]
                                                               [ Tactical EOC Command ]
                                                                          |
                                                               [ OSRM Safe Corridors ]
</pre>
<h2>6. Non-Functional Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Latency:</strong> Real-time event streaming latency under 200 ms via WebSocket feeds; vector tile rendering at 60 fps in MapLibre.</li>
<li><strong>Reliability:</strong> Fault-tolerant architecture with automated API fallbacks during degraded network conditions.</li>
<li><strong>Security:</strong> AES-256 encrypted payload transmission over TLS 1.3; strict sanitization of incoming geolocation coordinates.</li>
<li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Horizontal scaling of FastAPI workers to handle high concurrency during mass flood events.</li>
</ul>
</body>
